  "summary": "Augusta County Sheriff Donald Smith defended the county's two Flock ALPR cameras before the Board of Supervisors, citing anecdotal investigative successes despite data showing 182 searches from 3.5 million reads (a .005% hit rate). Supervisor Scott Seaton had earlier raised concerns about the low hit rate, and the sheriff pledged to weigh privacy concerns while continuing to review the program.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "the dataset reported 182 searches from the 3,495,807 vehicle reads for the 2026 year-to-date, which would be a hit rate of .005 percent",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    },
    {
      "quote": "The Flock system is secured to meet federal and military standards. Access to the system is strictly controlled, monitored, and logged. This system is then audited by the Sheriff's Office and the Virginia State Police.",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "I will continue to review how the system is used, weigh its benefits and limitations, and thoughtfully consider community concerns before making decisions about Flock cameras' future usage in Augusta County.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    }
  ],
